## 1. DEFINITIONS\
\
In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:\
\
**1.1** "Agreement" means this Classification Services Agreement including all appendices and amendments.\
\
**1.2** "Classification Services" means the services provided by the Society as described in Article 2.\
\
**1.3** "Vessel(s)" means the ship(s) owned or operated by the Company and subject to classification by the Society.\
\
**1.4** "Rules" means the Bureau Veritas Rules for the Classification of Steel Ships and any other applicable rules, regulations, and standards published by the Society.\
\
**1.5** "Certificate(s)" means any certificate, document, or statement issued by the Society in relation to the Classification Services.\
\
---\
\
## 2. SCOPE OF SERVICES\
\
**2.1 Classification Services**\
\
The Society agrees to provide the following Classification Services for the Vessels:\
\
- Initial classification surveys\
- Periodical surveys (Annual, Intermediate, Special, Renewal)\
- Continuous surveys\
- Damage surveys\
- Additional surveys as requested by the Company\
- Issuance and maintenance of classification certificates\
- Technical support and consultation\
\
**2.2 Statutory Services**\
\
Subject to authorization by flag state administrations, the Society may provide statutory certification services on behalf of flag states.\
\
**2.3 Additional Services**\
\
Additional services beyond the scope of standard classification may be provided upon request and subject to separate agreement.\
\
---\
\
## 3. OBLIGATIONS OF THE SOCIETY\
\
**3.1 Professional Standards**\
\
The Society shall:\
- Perform all services in accordance with its Rules and internationally recognized standards\
- Employ qualified and competent surveyors\
- Maintain professional independence and impartiality\
- Exercise reasonable skill and care in performing the services\
\
**3.2 Survey Scheduling**\
\
The Society shall:\
- Provide reasonable advance notice of survey requirements\
- Coordinate survey scheduling with the Company\
- Conduct surveys at locations mutually agreed upon\
- Minimize disruption to vessel operations where possible\
\
**3.3 Reporting**\
\
The Society shall:\
- Provide survey reports in a timely manner\
- Issue certificates upon satisfactory completion of surveys\
- Notify the Company of any conditions of class or recommendations\
- Maintain records in accordance with applicable regulations\
\
**3.4 Technical Support**\
\
The Society shall provide technical support and guidance regarding:\
- Interpretation of Rules\
- Survey requirements\
- Compliance with classification standards\
- Resolution of technical issues\
\
---\
\
## 4. OBLIGATIONS OF THE COMPANY\
\
**4.1 Vessel Maintenance**\
\
The Company shall:\
- Maintain the Vessels in accordance with the Rules\
- Implement all conditions of class within specified timeframes\
- Address recommendations in a timely manner\
- Ensure proper documentation is maintained\
\
**4.2 Survey Facilitation**\
\
The Company shall:\
- Provide safe access to all areas requiring inspection\
- Make available necessary equipment and personnel\
- Provide relevant documentation and records\
- Ensure vessel readiness for scheduled surveys\
\
**4.3 Notification**\
\
The Company shall promptly notify the Society of:\
- Accidents, casualties, or damage affecting class\
- Changes in vessel ownership or management\
- Changes in vessel name, flag, or particulars\
- Any modifications or alterations to the Vessel\
\
**4.4 Payment**\
\
The Company shall pay all fees in accordance with Article 5.\
\
---\
\
## 5. FEES AND PAYMENT\
\
**5.1 Fee Structure**\
\
Fees for Classification Services shall be based on:\
- Vessel type, size, and age\
- Scope of services required\
- Location of surveys\
- Society's published fee schedule\
\
**5.2 Payment Terms**\
\
- Invoices shall be issued following completion of services\
- Payment is due within thirty (30) days of invoice date\
- Late payments may incur interest charges\
- All fees are exclusive of taxes, which shall be borne by the Company\
\
**5.3 Additional Costs**\
\
The Company shall reimburse the Society for:\
- Travel and accommodation expenses for surveyors\
- Extraordinary expenses incurred in performing services\
- Costs associated with re-surveys due to vessel unreadiness\
\
**5.4 Fee Adjustments**\
\
The Society reserves the right to adjust fees annually with reasonable notice to the Company.\
\
---\
\
## 6. TERM AND TERMINATION\
\
**6.1 Term**\
\
This Agreement shall commence on January 1, 2025, and continue for a period of one (1) year, automatically renewing for successive one-year periods unless terminated.\
\
**6.2 Termination for Convenience**\
\
Either party may terminate this Agreement by providing ninety (90) days written notice to the other party.\
\
**6.3 Termination for Cause**\
\
Either party may terminate immediately upon written notice if:\
- The other party materially breaches this Agreement\
- The other party becomes insolvent or enters bankruptcy proceedings\
- Continuation of the Agreement becomes illegal or impossible\
\
**6.4 Effect of Termination**\
\
Upon termination:\
- All outstanding fees become immediately due\
- The Society shall provide final survey reports and documentation\
- Classification certificates may be withdrawn\
- Confidentiality obligations continue\
\
---\
\
## 7. LIABILITY AND INDEMNIFICATION\
\
**7.1 Limitation of Liability**\
\
The Society's liability under this Agreement shall be limited to:\
- Direct damages only\
- Maximum amount of fees paid for the specific service giving rise to the claim\
- Claims brought within one (1) year of the incident\
\
**7.2 Exclusions**\
\
The Society shall not be liable for:\
- Indirect, consequential, or punitive damages\
- Loss of profit, revenue, or business opportunity\
- Damages arising from reliance on certificates by third parties\
- Damages resulting from the Company's failure to maintain the Vessel\
\
**7.3 Indemnification**\
\
The Company shall indemnify and hold harmless the Society from:\
- Claims by third parties arising from the Company's operations\
- Claims resulting from the Company's breach of this Agreement\
- Claims arising from the Company's negligence or willful misconduct\
\
**7.4 Insurance**\
\
Each party shall maintain appropriate insurance coverage for its operations and liabilities.\
\
---\
\
## 8. CONFIDENTIALITY\
\
**8.1 Confidential Information**\
\
Both parties agree to:\
- Maintain confidentiality of proprietary information\
- Use confidential information only for purposes of this Agreement\
- Protect confidential information with reasonable security measures\
- Not disclose confidential information without prior written consent\
\
**8.2 Exceptions**\
\
Confidentiality obligations do not apply to information that:\
- Is publicly available\
- Was known prior to disclosure\
- Is independently developed\
- Must be disclosed by law or regulation\
\
**8.3 Data Protection**\
\
Both parties shall comply with applicable data protection and privacy laws.\
\
---\
\
## 9. GENERAL PROVISIONS\
\
**9.1 Governing Law**\
\
This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of Korea.\
\
**9.2 Dispute Resolution**\
\
Any disputes arising from this Agreement shall be resolved through:\
1. Good faith negotiations between the parties\
2. Mediation if negotiations fail\
3. Arbitration in accordance with the rules of the Korean Commercial Arbitration Board\
\
**9.3 Amendments**\
\
This Agreement may only be amended by written agreement signed by both parties.\
\
**9.4 Assignment**\
\
Neither party may assign this Agreement without prior written consent of the other party.\
\
**9.5 Force Majeure**\
\
Neither party shall be liable for failure to perform due to circumstances beyond reasonable control.\
\
**9.6 Notices**\
\
All notices shall be in writing and delivered to:\
\
